  "notes": "Used for birds, reptiles, fish, insects, and other egg-laying animals. Also functions as a suru verb ({孵化|ふか}する). Sometimes used figuratively for business incubation.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {孵化|ふか}する — to hatch\n- {孵化|ふか}{器|き} — incubator\n- {孵化|ふか}{率|りつ} — hatching rate\n- {人工|じんこう}{孵化|ふか} — artificial incubation\n- {孵化|ふか}{直後|ちょくご} — immediately after hatching\n\nUSAGE:\nIn business contexts, {孵化|ふか} is sometimes used metaphorically, similar to English \"incubation.\" An インキュベーター (incubator) supports new businesses, paralleling how an {孵化|ふか}{器|き} supports eggs.\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {羽化|うか} — emergence (of an insect from pupa to adult)\n- {産卵|さんらん} — egg-laying, spawning",
